---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';

// Deliberately describes what this site actually loads rather than the usual
// boilerplate: audited against the built output on 2026-09-04. The site sets no
// cookies of its own and runs no analytics, so saying it does would be worse
// than saying nothing. Third-party content is Google Fonts (every page), an
// Unsplash image host (41 pages) and one Google Maps embed (/contact).
//
// ⚠ The Maps embed is the only element that can set a cookie, and it does so
// as the page loads, without consent. Under PECR reg. 6 that needs prior
// consent, since a map is not "strictly necessary". Two ways to fix it: a
// consent banner, or make the map click-to-load. Click-to-load is simpler and
// removes the issue entirely — until one of them is done, this page has to
// describe the embed honestly, which is what it does below.
---

<LegalPage
  title="UK Vehicle Exporters Cookie Policy"
  description="What this website stores on your device and which third-party services it loads. We use no analytics, advertising or tracking cookies."
  heading="UK Vehicle Exporters Cookie Policy"
  crumb="Cookie Policy"
  updated="4 September 2026"
>
  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong>The short version:</strong> this website sets no cookies of its own, and we do not use analytics,
      advertising or tracking cookies of any kind. Two pieces of third-party content — a map on our contact page
      and the fonts the site is typeset in — are loaded from Google, and the map can set cookies in your
      browser. The detail is below.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What cookies are</h2>
  <p>
    A cookie is a small text file that a website asks your browser to store, so that something can be remembered
    between page loads. Similar technologies — local storage, session storage and tracking pixels — do much the
    same job. UK law (the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations) allows a site to store information
    on your device without asking only where it is strictly necessary to deliver a service you asked for.
    Anything else needs your consent first.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies we set</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>None.</strong> This site is a set of static pages. It has no login for visitors, no shopping basket
    and no session to remember, so there is nothing it needs to store on your device. We run no Google
    Analytics, no advertising pixels and no visitor-tracking software.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party content that loads on this site</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Service</th><th>Where</th><th>What it means for you</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Google Fonts</td>
          <td>Every page</td>
          <td>
            The site's typefaces are served by Google. Loading them sends your IP address and browser details to
            Google. Google states that it does not set cookies for the Fonts service.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Unsplash</td>
          <td>Photographs on many pages</td>
          <td>
            Some images are served from Unsplash's image host, which receives your IP address and browser
            details when the image loads.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Google Maps</td>
          <td>Our <a href="/contact">contact page</a> only</td>
          <td>
            The embedded map showing our Truro office is provided by Google and <strong>can set cookies in your
            browser as it loads</strong>. If you would rather it did not, do not open the contact page, or block
            third-party cookies for google.com in your browser settings. No other page loads a map.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Vercel</td>
          <td>Every page</td>
          <td>
            Our hosting provider serves the site and keeps standard server logs, including your IP address. It
            does not set cookies for visitors to this site.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Links to our Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, X, LinkedIn and WhatsApp pages are ordinary links, not embedded
    widgets. Nothing is loaded from those companies unless you click through, at which point their own policies
    apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Staff area</h2>
  <p>
    The content management system at <strong>/admin</strong> uses browser storage to keep our staff signed in.
    It is not part of the public site and nothing there applies to visitors.
  </p>

  <h2>Controlling cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Because we set none, there is no consent banner to change your mind on. If you want to control what
    third-party content can store, every major browser lets you block or delete cookies — look for Privacy or
    Site Settings in Chrome, Firefox, Safari or Edge. Blocking third-party cookies will not stop this site
    working; at most the contact page map may not display.
  </p>
  <p>
    If we later add anything that does set cookies — analytics, for example — we will ask for your consent
    before it loads, and update this page first.
  </p>

  <h2>More information</h2>
  <p>
    How we handle personal data more generally is set out in our{' '}
    <a href="/privacy-notice">Privacy Notice</a>. The Information Commissioner's Office publishes plain-English
    guidance on cookies at{' '}
    <a href="https://ico.org.uk/for-the-public/online/cookies/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
    Any question about this policy can go to{' '}
    <a href="mailto:sales@vehicleexports.co.uk">sales@vehicleexports.co.uk</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
